WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.167
The frontier watchlist.

2
00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:07.167
One idea each on what's cresting, enough to nod along and know what to look up.

3
00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.967
Diffusion transformers swap the U-Net for a transformer.

4
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:16.200
The transformer becomes the denoising backbone inside diffusion.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.200
It's the architecture behind Sora-class video and SD3 or Flux-class image models.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.767
Flow matching is a cleaner generative objective than classic diffusion.

7
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:33.700
You learn a straight-line flow from noise to data, which means fewer sampling steps and simpler math.

8
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.667
It powers Flux and modern audio generators.

9
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:41.667
Latent consistency is about generating in very few steps.

10
00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:46.267
You start with a diffusion model that needs thirty or more steps, and distill it.

11
00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.177
The result generates in one to four steps.

12
00:00:49.177 --> 00:00:52.533
That's what makes real-time image generation possible.

13
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:56.200
Voice AI is moving to speech-to-speech.

14
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:07.533
Native audio-in, audio-out models, like GPT-4o realtime and Gemini Live, replace the clunky speech to text, LLM, text to speech chain.

15
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:14.800
They enable real-time voice agents that handle interruptions, and they're exploding commercially in support and sales.

16
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.533
Video understanding means vision language models that take video directly.

17
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:24.700
Gemini-class models can hold hour-long video in context.

18
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.200
Use cases include surveillance, sports, and field-service inspection.

19
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.500
Edge AI runs small models on phones and laptops.

20
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:41.170
Think Phi, Gemma, or Qwen at half a billion to three billion parameters, via GGUF and llama.

21
00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:44.133
cpp, or Apple and Android NPU stacks.

22
00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:46.767
You gain privacy and lower latency.

23
00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.967
And there's zero API cost.

24
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:53.000
World models learn how an environment behaves.

25
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.067
They predict what happens next.

26
00:01:55.367 --> 00:02:01.567
It's the research bet, with Genie-class models and robotics, on how agents get real planning ability.

27
00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:07.700
Small language models are the under ten billion parameter class, chosen on purpose.

28
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.867
Fine-tuned specialists beat giant generalists on narrow tasks, at about one percent of the cost.

29
00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.067
That's the economic argument behind fine-tuning.

30
00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.075
Let's recap.

31
00:02:19.075 --> 00:02:25.067
Image and video generation is moving to transformers, flow matching, and few-step models.

32
00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.367
Voice and video are going native.

33
00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.800
Edge AI and small models cut cost and latency.

34
00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.800
And world models are the research bet on planning.
